"cnrs":{
    "Does this patient have difficulty maintaining mental focus or sustained attention, make careless mistakes, or not attend to details? If the text only mentions that the patient is alert or oriented, or only mentions memory, respond \"not mentioned\". Ignore issues with focusing the eyes.":"attention a1",
    "Is this patient easily distracted? If the text does not mention distraction, or the patient is distracted only by pain, respond \"not mentioned\"":"attention a2",
    "Is this patient often \"on the go,\" acting as if \"driven by a motor\", restless, or difficult to keep up with? If the text does not mention restlessness or mentions it only in the context of trouble sleeping, respond \"not mentioned\"":"attention a3",
    "Does this patient feel compelled to perform habits that are excessive and repetitive, and become distressed when prevented from doing so? If the text does not mention repetitive habits or only mentions physical rigidity, respond \"not mentioned\"":"attention a4",
    "Does this patient feel driven to complete tasks or behave in a rigid, inflexible way according to specific, personal rules? If the text does not mention rigid thinking or behavior, respond \"not mentioned\"":"attention a5",
    "Does this patient worry repeatedly or too much about his/her own emotional/physical state, in a way that seems excessive or inappropriate? If the text does not mention worries that are excessive or inappropriate, only mentions reasonable concerns about their health, or does not mention what the patient is worried about, respond \"not mentioned\".":"attention b6",
    "Does this patient repeat the same response (e.g., word, phrase, gesture, behavior) despite being ineffective or inappropriate? If the text does not mention repetitive behavior, respond \"not mentioned\"":"attention b7",
    "Does this patient get mentally “stuck” or struggle to shift thoughts or mental focus from one activity or situation to another? If the text does not mention issues shifting focus, respond \"not mentioned\"":"attention b8",
    "Is this patient unable to stop repetitive thoughts, urges or images that seem to cause distress? If the text does not mention repetitive thoughts or urges, respond \"not mentioned\"":"attention b9",
    "Does this patient act hastily or carelessly in the moment without thinking (e.g., interrupting others, trouble waiting his/her turn). If impulsivity is not mentioned, or is only mentioned in the context of  hasty or impulsive gait or other movement issues, respond \"not mentioned\". ":"emotion a10",
    "Does this patient show rapid changes in emotion that are unrelated to the situation?":"emotion a11",
    "Does this patient cry and/or laugh inappropriately, without an apparent trigger or cause? If the text does not mention crying or laughing, or only mentions crying or laughing in appropriate situations, respond \"not mentioned\".":"emotion a12",
    "Is this patient overly anxious, and/or do they experience sudden episodes of intense fear or discomfort (e.g., heart racing, shortness of breath)? If anxiety is not mentioned or only depression is mentioned, respond \"not mentioned\".":"emotion a13",
    "Does this patient show lack of pleasure from activities or interactions that used to be enjoyable? If the text does not mention enjoyment of activities, respond \"not mentioned\"":"emotion b14",
    "Does this patient show negative attitudes or pessimism about the future and a sense of hopelessness? If the text does not mention pessimism or hopelessness, respond \"not mentioned\". If the text indicates that a drug or treatment is improving their negative attitudes, respond \"yes\"":"emotion b15",
    "Is this patient uneasy or generally dissatisfied with life? If the text does not mention depressive symptoms, respond \"not mentioned\"":"emotion b16",
    "Does this patient seem very sad or depressed? If the text does not mention overall mood, respond \"not mentioned\". If the text indicates that the patient is being treated for depression, respond \"yes\"":"emotion b17",
    "Does this patient make repetitive movements, postures, or utterances that follow a particular pattern (e.g., hand flapping, finger flicking, body rocking, repeating noises or phrases)? Ignore cases of involuntary tremor. If the text does not mention repetitive movements, respond \"not mentioned\"":"autism a18",
    "Is this patient drawn to sensory experiences, such as excessive smelling or touching of objects, or fascination with lights or spinning objects? If the text does not mention sensory-seeking, respond \"not mentioned\"":"autism a19",
    "Does this patient avoid or show high sensitivity to texture (including clothing and the mouth-feel of foods)? If the text does not mention sensitivity to texture, or only mentions food sensitivities in relation to trouble swallowing, respond \"not mentioned\"":"autism b20",
    "Is this patient easily overwhelmed by, or has an extreme reaction to, sounds, textures, tastes, smells, temperature or lights? If the text does not mention sensitivity to stimulation, or only mentions food sensitivities in relation to trouble swallowing, respond \"not mentioned\"":"autism b21",
    "Does this patient communicate in a way that is difficult to follow, illogical, rambling, or nonsensical? If the text does not mention communication, or if the issues are only related to speech issues such as dysarthria rather than psychological, respond \"not mentioned\"":"psychosis a22",
    "Does this patient express irrational concerns or false beliefs that he/she is threatened in some way (e.g., others are out to hurt him/her)? If the text does not mention false beliefs or paranoia, respond \"not mentioned\"":"psychosis a23",
    "Does this patient see or hear things that they believe are real but are not mentioned? If the text does not mention hallucinations, respond \"not mentioned\"":"psychosis a24",
    "Does this patient have trouble understanding other people's feelings or perspective? If the text does not mention the patient's social interactions, respond \"not mentioned\"":"psychosis b25",
    "Does this patient appear distant or aloof, with a lack of emotional reactivity to situations or others that would typically evoke an emotional response? If the text does not mention the patient's emotional responses to situations, respond \"not mentioned\"":"psychosis b26",
    "Is this patient disinterested, unconcerned, or indifferent to daily activities, future events, self, or others? If the text does not mention disinterest or indifference, respond \"not mentioned\"":"psychosis b27",
    "Doeås this patient act or appear to be unreasonably angry or aggressive? If the text does not mention anger or aggression, respond \"not mentioned\"":"social a28",
    "Is this patient easily angered or irritable? If the text does not mention irritability, or only mentions irritability as a medication side effect, respond \"not mentioned\"":"social a29",
    "Is this patient intolerant of people entering their personal space or overly assertive or protective about communal space and objects? If the text does not mention social difficulties, respond \"not mentioned\"":"social a30",
    "Is this patient deliberately disobedient, defiant, or argumentative? If the text does not mention argumentativeness or defiance, respond \"not mentioned\"":"social a31",
    "Does this patient act in a passive, immature, or childlike manner If the text does not mention the patient's behavior, respond \"not mentioned\"?":"social b32",
    "Does this patient seem unaware of social cues, or speak or behave in a way that is inappropriate to the situation? If the text does not mention social cues or appropriateness, respond \"not mentioned\"":"social b33",
    "Does this patient seem unaware of others' personal space, have difficulty adapting to social situations, or act or make statements in a socially inappropriate manner? If the text does not mention social difficulties or inappropriate behavior, respond \"not mentioned\"":"social b34",
    "Is this patient overly trusting of others, vulnerable to being tricked or manipulated, or prone to believe highly unlikely statements or claims? If the text does not mention trustfulness or gullibility, respond \"not mentioned\"":"social b35"
    },
"hbs_seizure":{
    "Has this patient had a seizure? For example, the text may mention epilepsy, convulsions, or fits. If none of these are mentioned in the text, respond \"not mentioned\" instead of \"no\".":"seizure"
    }
}